Implementation details:
- Use urllib with UA and timeout, retries (2), save raw bytes.
- Parse arXiv Atom with xml.etree.ElementTree.
- Parse Semantic Scholar JSON and INSPIRE JSON.
- Normalization function: NFKC, remove $...$ math delimiters but keep inner text, strip LaTeX commands like \mathcal, \cup, \ldots, \textit, \emph; replace \cup→union etc. Simpler: remove backslash-commands (\\[a-zA-Z]+), remove braces, remove punctuation except alnum/space, lowercase, collapse whitespace, map unicode quotes/dashes to ascii.
- Longest common contiguous token run via difflib.SequenceMatcher(None, excerpt_tokens, fetched_tokens).find_longest_match → size. Also "coverage" = matched length / excerpt length.
- Threshold: contained if longest run >= 15 tokens OR coverage >= 0.6. Report both.
- Negative control: remove tokens in the matched span from fetched abstract, re-run → expect longest run < threshold.
- Token-shuffle control: deterministic shuffle (seeded) of fetched abstract tokens → expect not contained.
- Short-generic-phrase control: "we prove that for all" (6 tokens, threshold 15) → expect not contained.

